},
["GameObject-613823"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<This ancient runestone has a carving of several haranir standing on a forested mountain. They look below at another group of haranir following a ball that radiates wave-like energy. The ball is taking them deep underground to a cave filled with many roots.\r\n\r\nThis carving appears to depict a split within the Haranir society, leading to one group staying on the surface, while the other takes the journey to Harandar.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ancient Runestone",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 613823,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-553848"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Staff of Disintegration\r\n\r\nSome foes are only stopped when they are erased from existence. Such was Met'imua, an Amani who fought during the Troll Wars. He could regenerate so quickly that no blade, arrow, or spell could fell him. The Staff of Disintegration was crafted to overcharge arcane power, and used to eliminate every trace of Met'imua and his home.\r\n\r\nSo horrific was the carnage that both the staff and its creator were locked away, until it was taken by Grand Astromancer Capernian to Tempest Keep. The staff now rests in the light of the Sunwell, in hopes of cleansing its tragic past.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Staff of Disintegration",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 553848,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-252387"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "I should have admired Illidan from the beginning. After all, he saved my father's life.\r\n\r\nIt happened during a mission that Kur'talos took into the wilds beyond Black Rook Hold. I was not there to witness it, but it was reported that one of the Legion's ravenous felhunter demons attacked and disarmed my father. The beast would have devoured him if Illidan had not intervened. With his quick thinking and mastery of the arcane, the Stormrage twin defeated the demon and spared my father a grim end.\r\n\r\nRather than downplay this event, my father celebrated it. He named Illidan his personal sorcerer, and young Stormrage became the talk of the resistance. Moon Guard members clamored for an audience with him to discuss his thoughts on the war, the nature of demons, and the arcane arts. Before long, Illidan had gained a reputation as a sorcerer without equal.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "From that day forward, Illidan fought by my father's side in battle. I watched him like a storm crow, determined to learn more about this strange new member of my family's inner circle. \r\n\r\nWhat I discovered did not put my heart at ease. Far from it.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Dog-Eared Page",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 252387,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-613818"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "It was in the years that followed the rise of the ancient winged beasts that even we dared not hunt that the stone giants scoured our lands.\r\n\r\nWe knew of the poison in their ways and so we hid from their watching eyes. While some saw glory in tales of the stone armies banishing the ancient chaos that had covered the old world, we stayed away.\r\n\r\nWe had no interest in their great halls, or strange rituals. Our people listened to the song that came from within, not to the monotone staccato of their ordered march.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tarnished Mural",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 613818,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-620325"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<This set of tablets is old and weathered but seems like it has been well taken care of. However, only parts of them are legible.>\r\n\r\nPraise Akil'zon, whose covenant with our ruling family ensures our victory endures.\r\n\r\nPraise Jan'alai that our line of leaders through birth and death continues forever.\r\n\r\nPraise Halazzi for the clever Witherbark scribes who keep our records.\r\n\r\nPraise Nalorakk that these tablets, their archive, and our home that holds them never falls.\r\n\r\nAnd most of all praise ZUL'JIN who commissioned these tablets to renew our records and preserve our history that has been lost.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE SLOPES OF ZANDALAR\r\n\r\nCountless ages of our history have been lost either due to loss of elders keeping our oral traditions, or disasters and war.\r\n\r\nWhat is written here has been researched by Witherbark scholars and scribes commissioned by our warlord, ZUL'JIN.\r\n\r\nIN THE BEGINNING, the five (the Amani, the Witherbark, the Revantusk, the Shadowpine, and even the Vilebranch) tribes were one: THE AMANI--one family. And at the head was our patriarch MANZAJIN. He fought against the Zandalari, their greed, and their subjugation, to carve out borders of a new, free land.\r\n\r\nThe Amani continued for centuries in stability despite the Zandalari refusing to recognize the authority of the Amani tribe.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE MIGRATION\r\n\r\nThe names of MANZAJIN'S descendents have been lost, but what we do know is this: they pledged to rid the northeast of Kith'ix and the aqir and our bonds to the Zandalari.\r\n\r\nAs they traveled, they found their ability to call upon the loa weakened by the distance from their lands and the meddling of Kith'ix.\r\n\r\nEven so, their armies dispatched Kith'ix. The Amani cleansed the aqir from the land and created the vast Atal'Utek as a monument to their great battle but forbade entrance to its temple. \r\n\r\nWith this great victory began the AMANI EMPIRE OF ZUL'AMAN!",
},
{
["Page"] = 4,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE LOA OF ZUL'AMAN\r\n\r\nIt was in this time that the Amani became known to the loa of Zul'Aman and they to us. At first, we worshipped many, some worshipping still the loa of the Zandalari like Shadra and Hir'eek but, due to the distance, not often not receiving their blessing. Others worshipped minor loa.\r\n\r\nBut soon from the line of Zul'jin came the first Amani leader with the title hash'ey, Kindo'jan. Kindo'jan received the blessing of the four most powerful loa of Zul'Aman--Akil'zon, Halazzi, Jan'alai, and Nalorakk, and thus also the minor loa in the region.\r\n\r\nHe was so beloved of Akil'zon that from then on, the loa became not only the Loa of VICTORY but also the Loa of the Amani tribe and its leaders.\r\n\r\nKindo'jan commissioned the temple city of Atal'Aman and the temples Akil'alor, Jan'alor, Halaz'alor, and Nal'alor.",
},
{
["Page"] = 5,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE HASH'EY\r\n\r\nKindo'jan the hash'ey lived a long life spanning many generations. He established the order of the Loa Speakers and formalized the worshipful rituals we use still. Families began to group together near the temples of the loa that they worshipped most.\r\n\r\nThe Amani ruling family and others that worshipped Akil'zon settled in the temple city Atal'Aman and Amani'Zar.\r\n\r\nThe Witherbark settled in the region known as the Witherbark Bluffs.\r\n\r\nThe Shadowpine settled near Jan'alor and the islands around it, moving with the seasons.\r\n\r\nThe Revantusk settled near Nalorakk's Prowl.\r\n\r\nAnd the Vilebranch settled near Maisara, still clinging to the loa of the old lands.\r\n\r\nDespite living a long life, the hash'ey left no direct descendants, and encouraged his people to choose their next leader for their strength in mind, body, and spirit.",
},
{
["Page"] = 6,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: ATAI'NATHA\r\n\r\nDespite his wish, perhaps due to their love of Kindo'jan, ATAI'NATHA, distant relative of Kindo'jan from a colony near Zandalar, assumed the throne. He was conceited and vain in his appearance. He wore his scarlet hair long and had his tusks capped with gold and gems, in the style of the Zandalari.\r\n\r\nHe worshipped the loa, but they had no love for him. Akil'zon liked not the look in his eye, Halazzi the deception in his voice, Nalorakk his strange smell, and Jan'alai the darkness in his heart.\r\n\r\nThey were right to not trust him. He had a claw of precious gems and gold to wear made for him, but in secret, he had Vilebranch crafters use old, dark magic to give it power.\r\n\r\nWith it, he ruthlessly expanded Zul'Aman's borders, but also would use his claw to kill anyone who dissented. In the end, he was poisoned by his own servants at the urging of the chieftains of the other Amani tribes. \r\n\r\nHis claw was destroyed and so ended his life and rule.",
},
{
["Page"] = 7,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: REVANTUSK RISING\r\n\r\nThe death of Atai'natha left the Amani in disarray unril NOROBU THE SCARRED, general of the Amani and leader of the Revantusk, stepped forward to be tested--and won. After days of feasting and deliberating, Norobu was made leader.\r\n\r\nNorobu created a council consisting of the chief of each tribe and bade them to meet at Amani'Zar. \r\n\r\nDevout of Nalorakk, he knew war would come, but in the time between, decreed that the Amani fortify themselves.\r\n\r\nHe fortified Atal'Aman with stone, built walls, and commissioned the Throne of Manzajin: a place where the council could meet but also engage in sport, feasting, and celebration.\r\n\r\nNorobu, who held no ill will towards Atai'natha after his death, adopted his children, who revered him and never sought the throne.\r\n\r\nNorobu ushered in a new tradition of only the worthy of spirit, mind, and body ruling Zul'Aman.",
},
{
["Page"] = 8,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: BEFORE THE SUNDERING\r\n\r\nTheir names are lost, but based on ancient carvings, after Norobu's death, the duty of chieftain shifted from tribe to tribe, and our tribes--the Revantusk and the Witherbark--reached out in trade to other troll nations, establishing settlements of their own.\r\n\r\nLong after we settled away from Zandalar, we found war again--this time against our most hated foe: the elves. Before what the gokinye call \"The Sundering,\" the Pale Queen's empire spread far to the east, encroaching on our lands. Despite our skirmishes with them and mutual hatred, the Zandalari kings and Azshara struck a bargain, ceding land to them to end hostilities.\r\n\r\nWe saw this not as \"shrewd diplomacy,\" but as weakness.\r\n\r\nWhen the earth cracked, we thought the raging sea would keep the elves away, but they returned. They sacked the sacred burial site of our hash'ey, the markets of Tor'Yunta, and with magic created a new city--Silvermoon.\r\n\r\nOur hatred began anew.",
},
{
["Page"] = 9,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THALASSIAN WAR\r\n\r\nThe destruction of Tor'Yunta and the loss of Atal'Kindo caused us a great distress and sparked wars over years without number.\r\n\r\nFinally, Chieftain Tan'dani, a cunning strategist of the Witherbark tribe, led our forces into battle, slowly gaining ground in guerilla attacks but also suffering heavy losses.\r\n\r\nIt was then the Zandalari, from over the waters, offered us aid. They would help us regain our territory with nothing in return but good will.\r\n\r\nTan'dari saw through their offer. She knew that with their help came the eventual vassalage of the Amani Empire.\r\n\r\nBut during a diplomatic journey to meet with the Zandalari ambassadors, she disappeared. The Zandalari, with their belief in castes and hereditary rule, put a young but fierce Amani of royal blood--able to trace his line to Manzajin--on the throne.\r\n\r\nThus began the rule of JINTHA.",
},
{
["Page"] = 10,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: BATTLE FOR ATAL'KINDO\r\n\r\nWith JINTHA, heir of the Amani, back on the throne, the Amani set to scour the elven city conjured from air and the well from our lands. A combined army of both humans and elves poised to attack on different flanks.\r\n\r\nThinking the humans easy prey, Jintha attacked the humans on his southern flank, but fell into a trap made by the humans and elves there.\r\n\r\nJintha perished in the flames produced by the human mages. Seeing this, the Zandalari abandoned the fight and the Amani were forced to retreat behind the current boundary of Zul'Aman.\r\n\r\nIt is unclear who took over from Jintha as ruler, but it seems as though the role passed from the tribe again.\r\n\r\nFinally, ZUL'JIN of the AMANI was tested and began a new age.",
},
{
["Page"] = 11,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE REIGN OF ZUL'JIN\r\n\r\nThe reign of WARLORD ZUL'JIN marked a new beginning for our people ushering in an era of pride in our culture and a return as a world power.\r\n\r\nZul'jin reunited the tribes of the Witherbark, Revantusk, Shadowpine, and Vilebranch as one Amani.\r\n\r\nHe fought valiantly against the elves, keeping them off balance and away from Zul'Aman, always looking for a way to rid them from our lands for good.\r\n\r\nAfter being captured and rescued by the Horde, he allied with them in return for restoring our homeland.\r\n\r\nBut the Horde abandoned the fight and Zul'jin's army was pushed back by the elves in Doomhammer's War.\r\n\r\nYayo'jin the Mystic prophesied Zul'jin would harness a power greater than anyone had ever known and that the time of a new hash'ey was near.\r\n\r\nKnowing now that he can trust no one but his Amani, his advisor, Malacrass, wise hexpriest of the Vilebranch, has promised to help him secure the power to reclaim what's ours.",
},
{
["Page"] = 12,
["Text"] = "<It is clear that the etching on the top of the tablet has been ground down, and a sorrowful carving of a funeral procession has been carved on top of it. Based on the letters you can still discern underneath, you can tell this tablet was supposed to be on the continuation of Zul'jin's reign--not his death.>\r\n\r\nTHE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: THE DEATH OF ZUL'JIN\r\n\r\nOn the eve of obtaining the power to conquer the elves and return our lands, we were beset by an army of gokinye who invaded our temple city of Atal'Aman.\r\n\r\nOur warlord has died. Malacrass's body has not been recovered, and his only heir, Man'ye, the Aspect of Akil'zon, has died as well.\r\n\r\nWe know not what transpired within Atal'Aman. All that fought there are dead. Even the loa are silent in our defeat either in sorrow, anger, or shame.\r\n\r\nYoung ZUL'JARRA, Man'ye's daughter, already shows great promise. ZARAMA, her mother, will reign until she can be tested.\r\n\r\nLong live ZUL'JARRA long live ZARAMA.",
},
{
["Page"] = 13,
["Text"] = "THE RULERS OF ZUL'AMAN: \r\n\r\n<Much of the top of this tablet's text has been obliterated and recarved in a threatening motif of warriors with their tusks bared and their eyes wide.\r\n\r\nHowever, you can make out two chieftain entries. You believe the names are likely KAZRA'JIN and DAAKARA. You can also make out something referencing the name Zul.>\r\n\r\nDuring the turmoil that was beget by Zul'jin's death, the tribe fractured, some wanting to claim the power Zul'jin sought, others later to conquer abroad with the help of the Zandalari. They led many, but had selfish aims.\r\n\r\nThey were laid low by fate. Let no one mourn them! And let no one cross our borders under pain of death!",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "The Rulers of Zul'Aman",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 620325,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-620327"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Imagination! Child-like Wonder!\r\n\r\nThose protected by Filo must have both.\r\n\r\nBeware those would  harm children lest you stoke the ire of Filo and his brethren! Learn of Filo's dark side and nowhere but DEATH can you hide.\r\n\r\nFilo is called by many names:\r\n\r\nFirst Friend\r\n\r\nUncle Filo\r\n\r\nThe Guardian\r\n\r\n\r\nChildren have no need to worship, no need to call him. All Amani children earn his protection. The youngest child of every village is his speaker. Filo says nothing, but all understand.\r\n\r\nOther loa fear Filo's power. Nothing can kill him, and his rage is insatiable. But he is focused. Placid enough to eat from a child's hand but ruthless enough to kill the most powerful warrior if it suits him.\r\n\r\nFilo protects children beyond death. If a child dies before its mother or father, Filo and his attendants gather and wait with the child until their parents come to guide them.\r\n\r\nTo reach Filo, come to him and play. Only a child or the purest of heart hold him in sway.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tablet of Filo",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 620327,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-265818"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Har'alnor remains calm. Must keep an eye on the rutaani encampment: they seem more agitated today. Perhaps an outlier, but something to watch.\r\n\r\nPossibly related: the area around the roots have been infused with a new light. Strange. Unwelcome.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "It does not seem to be causing a problem as of yet, but I am suspicious of anything that I cannot verify with my own experiences. Where did this strange light come from? What is it doing? Who sent this?\r\n\r\nIt is my sacred duty as a Rootwarden to solve this problem. There are more frivolous among us who would rest on their laurels.\r\n\r\nAln'hara as my witness, the other elders will understand my wisdom.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ruia's Musings, Part 1",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 265818,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-555786"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "By order of Grand Magister Rommath, and ratified by Regent Lord Lor'themar Theron, the sin'dorei hereby bestow ownership of the Umbral Atrium to Magister Umbric and his ren'dorei in good standing with Silvermoon.\r\n\r\nLet none forget the sacrifice and heroism of the ren'dorei in Silvermoon's darkest hour.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Deed to the Umbral Atrium",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 555786,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-618558"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<This ren'dorei telescope seems at first like it's pointed in the direction of the distant Voidspire. When you put your eye to the lens, the telescope focuses in on a distant nest of flying beasts slightly to its left.\r\n\r\nThe armature of the stand is dotted in a fine mist of crimson blood and a shred of silver cloth in ren'dorei style. Claw marks mar the ground between your feet. They stretch all the way to the edge of the cliff and then disappear, pointed in the same direction as that nest.>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Abandoned Telescope",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 618558,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-613847"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<A haphazard collection of notes, diagrams, and letters documenting changes in the Dead Scar. Some writings are several years old, while others are more recent.>\r\n\r\nIt has been two months since my field experiment. The longer I sit with the knowledge that this taint is irreversible, the less I can bear it.\r\n\r\nPerhaps I made a mistake. The magistrix agreed with my research, but perhaps she was also mistaken.\r\n\r\nI have to keep looking.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "<Written on the back of a lengthy research log.>\r\n\r\nToday marks the end of a full year of testing. I have taken so many soil samples, stained more crates than I care to document, and yet I have nothing to show.\r\n\r\nSo many cleansing spells, draughts, runes. But still nothing will grow in that soil. No matter how carefully I tend to the seeds, they wither to ash within hours.\r\n\r\nIt cannot be hopeless. I refuse to let it be hopeless.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "<Scribbled at the bottom of a report dated years later:>\r\n\r\nI am so tired.",
},
{
["Page"] = 4,
["Text"] = "<A map of Quel'Thalas with a few frantically scribbled circles near the top of the Dead Scar.>\r\n\r\nPeacebloom shoots!",
},
{
["Page"] = 5,
["Text"] = "<Several diagrams of the Sunwell, accompanied by pages upon pages of complex magical equations.>\r\n\r\nThe growth started in the very north, but it has begun trickling southward over the past months.\r\n\r\nI found a few patches of grass as far down as the East Sanctum yesterday.\r\n\r\nGRASS!",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Mirveda's Notes",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 613847,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-620323"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Heart! Inner Fire!\r\n\r\nThose who follow Jan'alai have both.\r\n\r\nJan'alai--the dragonhawk that from ash lights the dawn, at birth and at death we hear their song.\r\n\r\nThey are called by many names.\r\n\r\nThe Everlasting Fire\r\n\r\nThe Twisting Flame\r\n\r\nThe Crucible\r\n\r\nThe Searing Truth\r\n\r\nThe Mistress and Master of Magic\r\n\r\nThe Shadowpine call upon Jan'alai to stoke their inner fire, fan the flames of their magic, fuel their desires. Life and death are under their wings, as are the songs her shamans sing. Jan'alai brings us life, ushers us through death and night, tracing the sun on its journey through time. The hatchling, the sage--they are one in the cycle of the dragonhawk loa, Jan'alai, patron of life, death, renewal, magic, and the FIRE in all Amani hearts!",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tablet of Jan'alai",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 620323,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-140262"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "FOR SALE: EZ-123 BUNKER BUILDER\r\n\r\nThe end is approaching, but you and your loved ones can survive with your very own B.B.! The Bunker Builder is the latest in gnomish engineering. Simple to operate, small enough for a mountain ram to carry, the B.B. can deploy in almost any terrain (see disclaimers). With the press of a button, the device will tunnel deep underground and hollow out a cozy cavern where you can live in peace. Each purchase comes with two air fresheners, a rope ladder (see disclaimers), and an operator's manual.\r\n\r\nDisclaimers: Not for use in sand, water, or Dalaran. Deploy rope ladder BEFORE entering the B.B. tunnel.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Tattered Pamphlet",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 140262,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["Item-265819"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Disgusting! Irresponsible! Reprehensible!\r\n\r\nIt would be the surface dwellers who would taint the sanctity of Harandar with their curses.\r\n\r\nTheir light spreads across the land like an infection blooming across our pristine fields, inciting the afflicted rutaani to madness. It must be stopped before it goes any further... and before the other elders hear that it happened on my watch.\r\n\r\nNo matter. A haranir will succeed where others have failed. This is a certainty.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Ruia's Musings, Part 2",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 265819,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-466230"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG ONE\r\n\r\nDornogal. It feels like I know this place, but I'm experiencing it for the first time. I don't quite understand it. \r\n\r\nI've talked to many of my kin, and they've explained as much as they could, but it hasn't helped at all. \r\n\r\nThis is my home, but it doesn't feel that way. \r\n\r\nI wonder if it ever will.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG TWO\r\n\r\nAs the days go by, attitudes seem to be changing. My kin can be rigid and stubborn, but there's a warmth to them.\r\n\r\nI've learned about what led to my day of awakening. Tribulations that lasted millennia.  \r\n\r\nI've awoken during a shifting age. I wonder what this means for me. Where is my place?",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG THREE\r\n\r\nSpeaker Brinthe insists I come up with a name for myself. I've toyed with different names. \r\n\r\nAurora? It doesn't quite fit, but it's what I saw before I woke.  I will never forget that beautiful light, the warmth of that voice.  \r\n\r\nMaybe something vibrant like Coral?\r\n\r\nNo, that doesn't quite fit either. I'll keep thinking.",
},
{
["Page"] = 4,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG SIX\r\n\r\nI feel less hesitant now. Adjusting to our society and all the rules has proven difficult. \r\n\r\nAs much as I love my kin, I still can't quite understand their adherence to tradition. They say it's what you're supposed to do. \r\n\r\nWhy? \r\n\r\nWhen I asked Brinthe, she had a different answer. At one point we served the Titans. \r\n\r\nBut now? \r\n\r\nNow we choose to serve one another. This has inspired me.",
},
{
["Page"] = 5,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG NINE \r\n\r\nMy name is Dawn. \r\n\r\nI had to write this down. It came to me after watching the sun rise over Dornogal.\r\n\r\nDawn, the start of a new day, of a new age. The end of darkness, the beginning of something more. \r\n\r\nThis I feel represents who I wish to be.",
},
{
["Page"] = 6,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG TEN\r\n\r\nI've been helping the Foreman quite a bit. He has been teaching about the rigid processes that my kin used to experience. \r\n\r\nThe machines don't seem to do well with we Awakened. \r\n\r\nAnd the Foreman's language at times can be harsh. I know he doesn't mean it in that way. \r\n\r\nThank the cogs that Caretakers exist. They seem to be a bit more prepared. \r\n\r\nIt takes time to change your ways--but I hope the Foreman adjusts sooner rather than later.",
},
{
["Page"] = 7,
["Text"] = "PERSONAL LOG TWELVE\r\n\r\nNext week I start implementing my improvements to the Awakening Protocol.\r\n\r\nI hope that they go well. Our awakening shouldn't be frightening. It should feel the same as the song's warm embrace. \r\n\r\nNo matter what happens, I do know this is a step into a new age. \r\n\r\nOne day earthen will travel beyond the shores of Khaz Algar. But for now, the first step.  \r\n\r\nOur society is changing. But there's no reason it must all be at once.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Navigations of the Soul",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 466230,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-553839"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "Devastation\r\n\r\nWarriors of the sin'dorei are normally known for spear, bow, and sword, but Thaladred the Darkener preferred an axe above all. First used during the Troll Wars, Devastation struck its enemies with such brutality that their swift regeneration, magic, and even calls to their loa would fail them.\r\n\r\nAlthough its origins lay in defense of Quel'Thalas, Thaladred wielded the weapon in service of the traitor Prince Kael'thas in later years. In doing so, he betrayed his people and forever stained the weapon's legacy. Until a day when one is found with the unique temperament to wield it, Devasation bathes in the light of the Sunwell, in the hopes of removing the Darkener's shadow.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Devastation",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 553839,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-579238"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "I have ignored the risks. When I was in the painting of a battle, some dark creature lashed out. I am still fevered from its venom.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "These are no mere visions, and they're more than memories. Ribs are broken, and the venom nearly reached my heart. But the rewards seem worth the price.",
},
{
["Page"] = 3,
["Text"] = "I must share my secrets, and train the next generation to be wiser than I was. Create, learn, and share--but temper and be aware. Each image can bring ruin. Each memory can bring death. And the Alndust is too precious to waste. Only a few will carry this honor, to let others live our past.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Echoes of Our Past--Part 3: Dangerous Memories",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 579238,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-245381"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "<HTML><BODY>\r\n<BR/><BR/>\r\n<H1 align=\"center\">Uther the Lightbringer</H1>\r\n<IMG src=\"Interface\\Common\\spacer\" align=\"center\" width=\"1\" height=\"27\"/>\r\n<P>\r\nFirst paladin, father of the original Order of the Silver Hand, guiding light for all. May we honor his legacy in all that we do.\r\n</P>\r\n</BODY></HTML>",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Uther the Lightbringer",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 245381,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-369228"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "ARCHIVIST ROH-LUDA, RELIC RESTORER\r\n\r\nThe afterlives of the Shadowlands give rise to many curious, fantastic, and unstable relics. It is our Purpose to catalog, curate, study, and safeguard them.\r\n\r\nBy our ministrations, we will better understand the nature of each afterlife, we will comprehend how disparate souls fit in the fabric of existence, and perhaps most importantly, we will keep potentially dangerous relics out of the hands of those who would misuse them.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Archivist Roh-Luda's Teachings",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 369228,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["Item-238500"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "The rules of nature reign supreme upon this world. Every species we've stumbled upon seems designed to fight and kill. Those that aren't purely carnivores feast instead on flows of Void energy. Perhaps we ren'dorei aren't so unlike them.\r\n\r\nThis is no homeworld of Void from what we can tell. It seems instead a planet, like any other, that exists at the nexus of Void energies throughout the cosmos. I am reminded of Outland. I advise similar survival tactics to those used by our kin who called themselves Sunfury before embracing the Void. We might ask Leona Darkstrider what she learned from Adarus Duskblaze.\r\n\r\nExploring the wastes remains a high priority. Natural resources born of this world are sure to be potent in our fight against Xal'atath.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Maella's Report",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 238500,
["Type"] = "Item",
},
},
["GameObject-252386"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "I first met Illidan in the early stages of the war, back when I considered the Burning Legion a passing threat. The night elf resistance was headquartered at my family's ancestral home, the great fortress of Black Rook Hold. Those days were glorious to behold. Thousands of elves gathered at the stronghold from the far ends of the empire, all sworn to defend our lands against the demons.\r\n\r\nAs the daughter of Commander Ravencrest, I enjoyed a position of power and privilege. I attended council meetings with sorcerers from the Moon Guard, priestesses from the Sisterhood of Elune, and other influential figures. I also crossed paths with lesser-known resistance members-elves like Illidan.",
},
{
["Page"] = 2,
["Text"] = "Illidan came to Black Rook Hold with his brother, the druid Malfurion Stormrage, and the priestess Tyrande Whisperwind. I met the trio only briefly, and they did not leave any lasting impressions on me. Illidan in particular seemed like just one more sorcerer among the hundreds who had joined the resistance.\r\n\r\nYet soon, everyone would know his name. And some, like me, would come to distrust him.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "Worn-Edged Page",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 252386,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
["GameObject-556449"] = {
["Text"] = {
["enUS"] = {
{
["Page"] = 1,
["Text"] = "We the undersigned agree to the following compact. That in times of great need and world ending threats, past grievances and vengeance can be set aside to allow the greatest minds of might and magic to come together and find solutions to craft war against such threats.\r\n\r\nLet all who follow this compact use this magic and wisdom for the betterment and defense of Azeroth and her citizens.\r\n\r\nIn the face of evil that threatens Azeroth herself, let those practitioners of magic once again work together for a better future.\r\n\r\nIn memory of Theramore, Dalaran, and the Sunwell.\r\n\r\nQuel'falan danas! \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSigned,\r\n\r\nVereesa Windrunner                                  Aethas Sunreaver\r\n\r\n\r\nWitnessed by Gyre.",
},
},
},
["Title"] = {
["enUS"] = "The Silversun Compact",
},
["Source"] = {
["ID"] = 556449,
["Type"] = "GameObject",
},
},
},
